BC-250: experimental VCN 2.0.3 ungate — staged bring-up + EFI breadcrumb

amdgpu.bc250_vcn_ungate=0  stock: VCN untouched (default)
                          =1  reg-only: register IP block, skip early/sw_init
                          =2  probe: + ucode parse + sw_init, zero VCN MMIO;
                             VCN ucode is never submitted to the PSP (CSF2
                             PSP returns ITEM_NOT_FOUND for LOAD_IP_FW 13)
                          =3  full: real bring-up. Each stage logs a
                             breadcrumb, persists the step name to the EFI
                             var BC250VcnStep (survives a full CPU stall),
                             then settles 200ms.

After a =3 wedge, boot normally and read
/sys/firmware/efi/efivars/BC250VcnStep-* : it holds the last completed
stage; the killing MMIO is the next one in the sequence.
